            "lead": "Implementing Zero Trust with Micro- segmentation 1",
            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<h3>Implementing Zero Trust with</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">Micro- segmentation 1</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>Zero Trust security strategy to reduce your organization&#x27;s cyber risk and exposure to attacks. Zero trust is restricting access to systems and resources to only what is required. Following network authentication, each request is checked against established access control policies and either granted or denied. Access to apps is allowed based on business logic and is limited to minimal essential permissions. Enforcing zero trust security necessitates the use of micro-segmentation. Micro-segmentation creates boundaries between workloads, allowing for stringent access control enforcement. This decreases network system susceptibility. Also, it limits an attacker&#x27;s access during a successful attack. https://www.cisco.com/site/us/en/learn/topics/security</p></div>",
