            "title": "What can micro-segmentation do that a firewall cannot?",
            "eyebrow": "CIT 220 • Unit 02",
            "subtitle": "Zero Trust & Microsegmentation Integration",
            "lead": "What can micro-segmentation do that a firewall cannot? Micro-segmentation goes beyond a firewall by applying granular security policies at the",
            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<h3>What can micro-segmentation do that a firewall cannot?</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">Micro-segmentation goes beyond a firewall by applying granular security policies at the</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>individual workload level, even within the same subnet, to prevent lateral threat movement and contain breaches, whereas firewalls typically focus on broad network perimeter control. Micro-segmentation provides enhanced security by creating isolated, secure zones for applications and servers, reducing the overall attack surface and supporting a zero- trust security model more effectively than traditional firewalls alone.</p></div>",
            "cleanText": "What can micro-segmentation do that a firewall cannot? Micro-segmentation goes beyond a firewall by applying granular security policies at the individual workload level, even within the same subnet, to prevent lateral threat movement and contain breaches, whereas firewalls typically focus on broad network perimeter control. Micro-segmentation provides enhanced security by creating isolated, secure zones for applications and servers, reducing the overall attack surface and supporting a zero- trust security model more effectively than traditional firewalls alone.",
