            "lead": "2.3 Virtual Private Networks (VPNs) CIT 220 - Information Assurance and Security 2",
            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<h3>2.3 Virtual Private</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">Networks (VPNs) CIT 220 - Information Assurance and Security 2</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>VPN stands for &quot;Virtual Private Network&quot; and describes the opportunity to establish a protected network connection when using public networks. VPNs encrypt your internet traffic and disguise your online identity. This makes it more difficult for third parties to track your activities online and steal data. The encryption takes place in real time. https://www.kaspersky.com/resource-center/definitions/what-is-a-vpn</p></div>",
            "cleanText": "2.3 Virtual Private Networks (VPNs) CIT 220 - Information Assurance and Security 2 VPN stands for \"Virtual Private Network\" and describes the opportunity to establish a protected network connection when using public networks. VPNs encrypt your internet traffic and disguise your online identity. This makes it more difficult for third parties to track your activities online and steal data. The encryption takes place in real time. https://www.kaspersky.com/resource-center/definitions/what-is-a-vpn",
