            "title": "Here's a breakdown of VPN examples:",
            "eyebrow": "CIT 220 • Unit 02",
            "subtitle": "Virtual Private Networks (VPNs) & Protocols",
            "lead": "Here's a breakdown of VPN examples: VPN Protocols These are the underlying technologies used to create a secure connection",
            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<h3>Here&#x27;s a breakdown of VPN examples:</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">VPN Protocols These are the underlying technologies used to create a secure connection</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>over a public network.  OpenVPN: A widely used, open-source VPN protocol.  WireGuard: A newer, faster, and more modern VPN protocol.  IPsec (Internet Protocol Security): A suite of protocols that provides authentication and encryption.  L2TP/IPsec (Layer 2 Tunneling Protocol): A common VPN tunneling protocol often paired with IPsec.  SSL/TLS (Secure Socket Tunneling Protocol): Used in web-based VPNs to provide encrypted access to applications and data.</p></div>",
            "cleanText": "Here's a breakdown of VPN examples: VPN Protocols These are the underlying technologies used to create a secure connection over a public network.  OpenVPN: A widely used, open-source VPN protocol.  WireGuard: A newer, faster, and more modern VPN protocol.  IPsec (Internet Protocol Security): A suite of protocols that provides authentication and encryption.  L2TP/IPsec (Layer 2 Tunneling Protocol): A common VPN tunneling protocol often paired with IPsec.  SSL/TLS (Secure Socket Tunneling Protocol): Used in web-based VPNs to provide encrypted access to applications and data.",
